export default "Ragly (\"Ragly\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\") is a pet care and discovery platform operated under the Ragly brand from the Republic of Moldova.\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, disclose, and protect personal information when you use the Ragly mobile application, the Ragly website, and related services (collectively, the \"Service\").\n\n### Data controller\n\nThe data controllers of personal information processed through Ragly are the following natural persons, who act as joint controllers:\n\n- Yoav Shamir\n- Michael Sigal\n- Konstantine Staver\n\nTogether they decide why and how personal information is processed in Ragly. There is no separate registered company under the Ragly brand at the date of this Policy.\n\nEssential allocation of responsibilities between the joint controllers:\n\n- Privacy requests and data subject rights (access, correction, deletion, and related requests): handled jointly through the single contact point below. Any of the three controllers may answer; the reply is given on behalf of all of them.\n- Day-to-day data security and technical safeguards for the app, servers, and websites: Yoav Shamir, with the others informed of material risks and incidents.\n- Contracts and relationships with third-party processors and service providers: decided jointly; practical administration is handled by Yoav Shamir.\n- Personal data breaches: any controller who becomes aware of a suspected breach must inform the others without delay. Notifications to authorities and users, where required, are coordinated jointly and sent from the contact point below.\n- Users may exercise their rights against any of the joint controllers. Using the contact point below is enough; you do not need to contact each person separately.\n\nPrivacy contact: support@ragly.cloud\nPostal address: Bd. Traian 7/1, Chisinau, Republic of Moldova, 2060\nWebsite: https://ragly.cloud\nCountry of establishment: Republic of Moldova\n\nYou must be at least 18 years old, or the age of legal majority in your country of residence if that age is higher, to create an account and use Ragly.\n\nWe handle personal information in accordance with applicable data protection laws, including Law No. 195/2024 of the Republic of Moldova on Personal Data Protection and, where they apply to you, the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the Israeli Protection of Privacy Law, 5741-1981, and its regulations.\n\nRagly is established in the Republic of Moldova and currently focuses on users in Moldova and Israel. Whether an EU or UK GDPR representative is required depends on how and where the Service is offered. We will update this Policy if a representative is appointed.\n\n## 1. Information We Collect\n\nWe collect information that you provide directly, information generated when you use the Service, and limited information received from service providers.\n\nThe information collected depends on the features you use and the permissions you grant.\n\n### 1.1 Account and Profile Information\n\nWhen you create or manage an account, we collect:\n\n- Name\n- Email address\n- Authentication information, such as one-time verification codes and sign-in tokens\n- Optional phone number\n- Optional profile photo\n- Account preferences and settings, such as language, theme, and notification settings\n\nYou sign in with a one-time code that we send to your email address. Ragly does not use passwords.\n\nYour name and email address are required to create an account. You can change or remove your phone number and profile photo in Settings → My profile.\n\n### 1.2 Pet Information and Care Records\n\nYou may choose to provide information about your pets, including:\n\n- Pet name and photo\n- Animal type and breed\n- Date of birth and age\n- Sex, weight, and color\n- Spay or neuter status\n- Microchip and passport numbers\n- Vaccination records and dates\n- Health topics, notes, and veterinary visit details\n- Medication and treatment information\n- Reminders\n- Photos attached to pet records\n\nWe use this information only to provide the pet-management features of Ragly. These are personal records that you enter; they are not clinic medical records.\n\nPet information may be personal information when it identifies you or can be linked to you.\n\nRagly does not use pet records to provide veterinary diagnosis or treatment.\n\n### 1.3 Location Information\n\nIf you allow location access, Ragly uses your device's precise location to find and sort nearby businesses and pet-friendly places.\n\nLocation access is optional. Ragly works without it, but nearby discovery will be limited.\n\nWhen you use nearby discovery, your device sends its current coordinates to our servers to calculate distances. We use them only to answer that request. We do not save your location to your account or keep a location history. Because the coordinates are part of the request, they appear in our server's technical request logs, which are deleted automatically after 30 days (see section 5).\n\nYou can turn location access off at any time in your device settings.\n\n### 1.4 Reviews, Ratings, and Public Content\n\nWhen you rate or review a business, we collect:\n\n- Your star rating\n- Your review text\n- Your name\n- Your profile photo, if you have one\n- The date and related technical information\n\nReviews are shown publicly in Ragly together with your name and profile photo.\n\nOther users can see, copy, or share content you publish.\n\nDo not include sensitive personal information, private medical details, financial information, or information about another person without their permission in a public review.\n\nYou can delete your own reviews in the app.\n\n### 1.5 Photos and Uploaded Files\n\nYou may upload photos, including:\n\n- Pet profile photos\n- Your profile photo\n- Vaccination proof images\n- Photos attached to pet records and notes\n\nWe store and process these files only to provide the features you use. Ragly does not support video uploads.\n\nPlease do not upload photos or documents that contain personal or confidential information unrelated to the purpose of the feature.\n\n### 1.6 Device and Technical Information\n\nWe collect limited technical information needed to operate, maintain, and secure the Service:\n\n- IP address, which our servers and service providers receive with every request\n- Device type, operating system, app version, language, and time zone\n- Push notification token, if you allow notifications\n- Notification preferences\n- A random installation identifier that Expo uses to deliver app updates\n- A Firebase Analytics app instance identifier, only while analytics is on (see section 1.7)\n- Your Ragly account identifier, which RevenueCat uses to link your subscription to your account\n- Server request logs: the time of each request, the IP address, the device and app version, the address requested (which for nearby searches includes location coordinates), and whether it succeeded\n\nRagly does not use crash-reporting tools such as Firebase Crashlytics, and it does not collect advertising identifiers (such as Apple's IDFA or Google's Advertising ID).\n\n### 1.7 Analytics and Usage Information\n\nRagly uses Google Firebase Analytics to understand how the app is used and to improve its reliability.\n\nThis includes:\n\n- App opens and sessions\n- Screens viewed and features used\n- Subscription and purchase events\n- General device and app information, such as device model, operating system, app version, language, and approximate country derived from your IP address\n\nFirebase Analytics links these events to a random app instance identifier, not to your name or email address. Google keeps analytics data for the retention period set in our Google Analytics settings (2 months for user-level data) and then deletes it.\n\nHow analytics is switched on or off:\n\n- Firebase Analytics is disabled in the app's native configuration until the app checks your preference. No analytics events or analytics identifiers are sent before that check.\n- If your device region is in the European Union, the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, Switzerland, or the Republic of Moldova, or if the region cannot be determined, analytics stays off until you choose Allow in the consent prompt. Closing the prompt counts as Don't allow.\n- In other regions, where the law permits, analytics is turned on by default after that check, without a consent prompt.\n- Your choice is stored only on your device (not on our servers). You can change it at any time in Settings → Usage analytics without deleting your account.\n- If you withdraw consent or turn analytics off, collection stops. Google may keep earlier analytics data for the retention period above. Turning analytics off does not delete historical analytics data already held by Google.\n- Firebase Analytics is the only analytics tool in the app. We do not use analytics data for advertising, and we do not track you across apps or websites owned by other companies.\n\n### 1.8 Subscription and Purchase Information\n\nIf you buy a subscription, we receive:\n\n- Subscription status and type\n- Purchase and renewal status\n- Entitlement information\n- Transaction identifiers\n- Purchase and expiry dates\n\nPurchases are processed by the Apple App Store or Google Play and managed through RevenueCat.\n\nRagly never receives or stores your payment card number. Payment information is handled by Apple or Google under their own privacy policies and terms.\n\n## 2. How We Use Your Information\n\nWe use personal information to provide, maintain, protect, and improve Ragly, including to:\n\n- Create, authenticate, and maintain your account\n- Provide pet profiles and record-management features\n- Store vaccination records, health topics, notes, and reminders\n- Show and sort nearby businesses and pet-friendly places\n- Show business ratings and reviews, together with the reviewer's name and photo\n- Send verification emails and other service messages\n- Send push notifications and reminders you set\n- Manage subscriptions and restore purchases\n- Provide customer support\n- Review reports and moderate user content\n- Investigate fraud, abuse, and violations of our Terms\n- Suspend or block accounts that violate our Terms\n- Keep the Service secure\n- Diagnose technical problems and improve performance\n- Comply with legal obligations and respond to lawful requests\n\nWe do not sell personal information.\n\nWe do not use personal information for third-party advertising or to track you across other companies' apps or websites.\n\n## 3. Legal Bases for Processing\n\nWhere data protection law requires a legal basis for processing, we rely on the bases below. The same activity may rely on more than one basis where the law allows it.\n\n### 3.1 Purpose and legal basis\n\n- Creating and managing accounts — performance of a contract\n- Storing pet profiles, vaccination records, health topics, notes, and reminders — performance of a contract\n- Sending reminders and push notifications you set — performance of a contract; device permission is based on consent\n- Nearby business discovery using location — performance of a contract for the feature you request; device location permission is based on consent\n- Processing subscriptions and entitlements — performance of a contract; related records may also be kept for legal obligations\n- Publishing and displaying reviews and ratings — performance of a contract and legitimate interests in operating a trustworthy discovery service\n- Moderating content, handling reports and blocks, and preventing abuse — legitimate interests; legal obligations where applicable\n- Responding to support and privacy requests — performance of a contract and/or legitimate interests\n- Firebase Analytics — consent where required (see section 1.7); elsewhere, legitimate interests in understanding and improving the Service where the law permits\n- Security, fraud prevention, and server request logs — legitimate interests and/or legal obligations\n\n### 3.2 Consent\n\nWhere we rely on consent, you can withdraw it at any time. This does not affect processing that took place before you withdrew it.\n\n### 3.3 Legitimate Interests\n\nWhen we rely on legitimate interests, we take your rights and interests into account and do not use this basis where your interests override ours.\n\n### 3.4 Required and Optional Information\n\nYou are not legally required to give us any information. Your name and email address are needed to create an account, and without them we cannot provide the Service. All other information is optional; if you do not provide it, only the related feature will be unavailable.\n\n### 3.5 Automated Decisions\n\nWe do not make decisions about you based solely on automated processing that produce legal effects or similarly significantly affect you.\n\n## 4. How We Share Information\n\nWe do not sell personal information.\n\nWe share information only with the following recipients, and only as needed to operate Ragly.\n\n### 4.1 Service Providers and Other Recipients\n\nDepending on the service, a third party may act as a data processor on our behalf, as an independent data controller, or as a service that receives limited data directly from your device or browser. Where a third party acts as an independent controller, its processing is governed by its own privacy policy and terms.\n\nProcessors acting on our instructions (under their data processing terms):\n\n- Google Cloud (Google) — runs our servers and keeps server request logs. Receives everything the app sends to our servers. Located in Belgium.\n- MongoDB Atlas (MongoDB, on Amazon Web Services) — our database. Stores your account, pet records, reminders, and reviews. Located in Sweden.\n- Resend — sends verification codes and other service emails. Receives your email address and the email content. Located in the United States.\n- Expo — delivers push notifications and app updates. Receives your push notification token, notification text, and the app update installation identifier. Located in the United States.\n- RevenueCat — manages subscriptions on our behalf. Receives your Ragly account identifier and purchase status from Apple or Google. Located in the United States.\n- Cloudflare — hosts and protects the Ragly websites. Receives website visitors' IP addresses and request details. Operates a global network.\n- Google Firebase Authentication, Cloud Storage, and Firebase Analytics (Google) — used to authenticate you, store photos you upload, and (while analytics is on) process analytics events. Processes data in the United States and other Google locations. For these services Google generally acts as our processor under Google's data processing terms. Google may also process limited information as an independent controller where required to provide and secure its platform, under Google's own privacy policy.\n\nIndependent controllers or services that receive data under their own policies:\n\n- Apple App Store and Google Play — app distribution, store accounts, and in-app purchases. They process payment and subscription data as independent controllers under their own privacy policies. Ragly never receives your payment card number.\n- OpenStreetMap / Nominatim — map tiles load directly in your browser from OpenStreetMap (your IP address is received by them). Address search text is sent by our server to Nominatim. These services operate under OpenStreetMap's policies.\n\nFor the processors listed above, Ragly relies on each provider's standard Data Processing Agreement (or equivalent processor terms), including Standard Contractual Clauses and/or Data Privacy Framework participation where those terms provide them. We have confirmed these terms for Google Cloud / Firebase, MongoDB Atlas, RevenueCat, Resend, Cloudflare, and Expo against Ragly's accounts.\n\n### 4.2 Other Users\n\nWhen you publish a review, it is visible to other Ragly users together with your name and profile photo.\n\nYour pet records and private account information are never made public.\n\n### 4.3 Listed Businesses\n\nRagly shows information about veterinary clinics, groomers, pet shops, pet pharmacies, and pet-friendly places.\n\nIf you contact a business directly, for example by phone, that business receives whatever you choose to share with it.\n\nRagly does not share your pet records with listed businesses. Businesses can see reviews published about them.\n\n### 4.4 Moderation and Safety\n\nWhen you report a review or a user, block a user, or when content you posted is reported, we process the relevant information to investigate and enforce our Terms.\n\nThis may include:\n\n- The reported content\n- The reporting user's account information\n- The reported user's account information\n- Related review and moderation history\n- Actions we take and our decisions\n- Other information reasonably needed to investigate safety or policy violations\n\nAuthorized Ragly administrators may access this information for moderation, security, and enforcement.\n\nWe keep these records for 2 years from the report, as described in section 5.1.\n\n### 4.5 Legal and Safety Disclosures\n\nWe may disclose information where reasonably necessary to:\n\n- Comply with laws, regulations, or legal processes\n- Respond to valid requests from competent authorities\n- Investigate suspected fraud, abuse, or illegal activity\n- Enforce our Terms of Service\n- Protect the rights, safety, and property of Ragly, our users, businesses, or others\n- Prevent imminent harm or respond to serious security incidents\n\n### 4.6 Business Transfers\n\nIf Ragly is involved in a merger, acquisition, restructuring, financing, sale of assets, or similar transaction, personal information may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to confidentiality and data protection requirements. We will notify you before your information becomes subject to a different privacy policy.\n\n## 5. Data Retention and Deletion\n\nWe keep personal information only for as long as needed for the purposes in this Policy, unless the law requires or allows us to keep it longer.\n\n### 5.1 Retention Periods\n\nWe keep each type of information for the following periods:\n\n- Account information (name, email address, phone number, profile photo, settings): while your account exists. Deleted when you delete your account.\n- Pet profiles, vaccination records, health topics, notes, and reminders: until you delete them or your account. Deletion from our database happens immediately.\n- Reviews and ratings: until you delete the review or your account. Deletion from our database happens immediately.\n- Photos and uploaded files (Firebase Storage):\n  - If you remove a photo from a pet profile, note, vaccine record, or your account profile, or you replace it with a new one, it stops appearing in the app immediately because we remove or replace the link in our database. The previous file in Firebase Storage may remain until you delete your account, or until you ask us by email to delete that specific file.\n  - If you delete a pet profile, its records stop appearing in the app immediately. Associated photo files in Storage are removed when you delete your account, or earlier on request by email.\n  - If you delete your entire account, we delete the Storage files under your account folder as part of that process.\n  - Residual copies may remain temporarily in provider-managed backups or system logs, subject to those providers' retention periods.\n- One-time verification codes: deleted automatically once they expire, within minutes.\n- Push notification tokens: until you turn off notifications on the device, the token changes, or you delete your account.\n- Reports and moderation records (the reported content, the people involved, and our decisions): 2 years from the report, so we can handle repeated abuse and appeals. We keep them longer only while they are needed for an ongoing dispute, legal claim, or request from an authority. These records are kept even if the account involved is deleted.\n- Server request logs: deleted automatically after 30 days.\n- Business listing statistics: the coded visitor identifiers used to count unique visitors are deleted after 90 days. The resulting totals do not identify anyone and are kept with the listing.\n- Messages sent through the contact form on the Ragly for Business website: 12 months.\n- Usage analytics: kept by Google for 2 months at user level, as described in section 1.7.\n- Subscription records: we keep your subscription status while your account exists. Apple, Google, and RevenueCat keep transaction records under their own retention policies (see section 5.3). Ragly does not issue invoices or hold payment records itself, because Apple and Google sell the subscription.\n\nRagly does not run its own separate database backup system. Our MongoDB Atlas cluster is on a free tier that does not provide Atlas continuous backups. Infrastructure providers (for example Google Cloud, Firebase, or Cloudflare) may still keep short-term technical copies, logs, or recovery snapshots under their own policies. Deleted information therefore leaves Ragly's active systems as described above, but may remain briefly in those provider-managed copies until they are overwritten.\n\n### 5.2 Account Deletion\n\nYou can delete your account:\n\n- In the Ragly app: Settings → Account → Delete account\n- On the web, without signing in: https://ragly.cloud/delete-account.html\n- By emailing support@ragly.cloud from the email address of your Ragly account\n\nWhen you delete your account in the app, we delete your account, pet records, reminders, reviews, push tokens, and stored photos from our active systems as part of that process. If you ask by email or through the webpage, we first verify that the request comes from you, and then complete the deletion within 30 days.\n\nWe keep information after deletion only where:\n\n- The law requires us to keep it\n- It is needed to resolve disputes or enforce legal rights\n- It is a moderation record described in section 5.1\n\nAny information we must keep is used only for the purpose it is kept for.\n\n### 5.3 Subscription and Purchase Records\n\nApple, Google, and RevenueCat keep their own subscription and purchase records under their own retention policies.\n\nDeleting your Ragly account does not delete records held by those providers and does not cancel an active subscription. You must cancel the subscription in your App Store or Google Play account.\n\n## 6. Your Privacy Rights and Choices\n\nDepending on where you live, you may have the right to:\n\n- Access your personal information\n- Correct inaccurate or incomplete information\n- Have your information deleted\n- Restrict certain processing\n- Object at any time to processing based on our legitimate interests\n- Withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent\n- Receive your information in a portable format\n- Complain to a data protection authority, such as the National Center for Personal Data Protection of the Republic of Moldova, the supervisory authority of the EU country where you live or work, or the Israeli Privacy Protection Authority\n\nTo use these rights, email support@ragly.cloud.\n\nWe may need to verify your identity before acting on a request. We respond within the time required by applicable law.\n\n### 6.1 Managing Your Information in Ragly\n\nIn the app, you can:\n\n- Update your name and profile information\n- Change or remove your profile photo\n- Remove your phone number\n- Edit or delete pet profiles\n- Delete vaccination records, health topics, notes, and reminders\n- Delete reviews you wrote\n- Report reviews or users that break our rules\n- Block users, so you no longer see their reviews\n- Turn usage analytics on or off\n- Change notification preferences\n- Turn off location access in your device settings\n- Delete your account\n\n## 7. International Data Transfers\n\nRagly is operated from the Republic of Moldova. Our servers run on Google Cloud in Belgium, and our database is hosted by MongoDB Atlas on Amazon Web Services in Sweden (both in the European Union). Our service providers, including Google Firebase, also process information in other countries, including the United States.\n\nYour information may therefore be transferred to, stored in, or accessed from countries outside your country of residence. Section 4.1 lists each provider and where it processes data.\n\nWe protect these transfers as follows:\n\n- Each provider processes personal information under a data processing agreement with us, based on its standard data processing terms.\n- For transfers from the European Union, the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland to a country without an adequacy decision, such as the United States, these agreements include the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses (with the UK and Swiss addenda where needed), or the provider is certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and its UK and Swiss extensions.\n- Transfers from the Republic of Moldova follow the requirements of Moldovan data protection law.\n- We also use technical safeguards such as encryption in transit and restricted access.\n\nThe joint controllers named above handle data protection requests and security incidents through support@ragly.cloud. If a personal data breach is likely to put your rights at risk, we notify the competent data protection authority and, where required, affected users, within the time limits set by law.\n\nYou can ask for a copy of the transfer safeguards that apply to your information by emailing support@ragly.cloud.\n\n## 8. Data Security\n\nWe use technical and organizational safeguards to protect personal information against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, loss, or destruction, including:\n\n- Encryption of data in transit\n- Access controls and authentication\n- Restricted access to production systems\n- Secure hosting with established cloud providers\n- Monitoring and technical diagnostics\n\nNo system, network, or method of storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.\n\nKeep access to your email account secure, and contact us right away if you suspect unauthorized access to your Ragly account.\n\n## 9. Children's Privacy\n\nRagly is for adults only. You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of legal majority in your country of residence if that age is higher, to create an account and use Ragly. Ragly is not directed to children or teenagers.\n\nWe do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we learn that we have collected personal information from a child, we will delete it.\n\nParents or guardians who believe a child has given us personal information can contact support@ragly.cloud.\n\n## 10. Ragly Websites\n\nThis Policy also covers our websites: ragly.cloud and the Ragly for Business website, where businesses manage their listings.\n\n- ragly.cloud is a static information site. It has no cookies, analytics, trackers, forms, or embedded content. Cloudflare, which hosts it, receives visitors' IP addresses and request details to deliver and protect the site.\n- The Ragly for Business website shows maps from OpenStreetMap. When a map is shown, your browser loads the map images directly from OpenStreetMap, which receives your IP address.\n- When you search for an address on the Ragly for Business website, our server sends the search text to OpenStreetMap's address search service (Nominatim). Your IP address is not sent to it.\n- If you send us a message through the contact form on the Ragly for Business website, we receive your name, email address, optional phone number, and IP address. We use them to reply and to prevent spam, and we keep them for 12 months.\n- Business accounts, listings, and the information businesses submit are also described in the Business Privacy Notice (https://ragly.cloud/business-privacy.html) and the Ragly Business Terms (https://ragly.cloud/business-terms.html).\n\n### 10.1 Cookies and similar technologies on the Ragly for Business website\n\n- `ragly_locale` — remembers the language you choose; lasts 1 year; functional. Set only after you choose a language. Not used for advertising or analytics.\n- Firebase Authentication session — keeps you signed in to the Business website; lasts until you sign out or the session expires; essential. Stored by Firebase in your browser (typically IndexedDB / local storage), not as a first-party HTTP cookie named by Ragly.\n\nThe Business website does not use advertising or analytics cookies. Because these technologies are limited to essential sign-in and a functional language preference, it does not currently show a cookie consent banner. If we add non-essential cookies later, we will update this section and, where required, ask for consent.\n\n## 11. Third-Party Websites and Services\n\nRagly may contain links to third-party websites, apps, maps, payment services, or business pages.\n\nThose services are operated independently and have their own privacy policies and terms. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, content, or security.\n\nPlease review their privacy policies before giving them personal information.\n\n## 12. Push Notifications\n\nIf you allow push notifications, Ragly stores your device's push notification token, time zone, and notification preferences so we can send reminders and service notifications.\n\nYou can manage notifications in Ragly's settings and in your device's settings.\n\nTurning notifications off means you will not receive reminder alerts.\n\nNotification delivery depends on Apple, Google, Expo, your network, and your device settings, which are outside our control.\n\n## 13. Analytics and Tracking\n\nRagly uses Google Firebase Analytics as described in section 1.7.\n\nWe do not sell personal information, show third-party ads, or track you across other companies' apps and websites for advertising.\n\nWhere the law requires it, we ask for your consent before analytics runs, and you can withdraw it at any time in Settings → Usage analytics.\n\nYour device may also offer its own privacy controls for analytics and tracking.\n\n## 14. Changes to This Privacy Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes to the Service, technology, legal requirements, or our data practices.\n\nIf we make material changes, we will notify you in the app, by email, or by another appropriate method.\n\nThe updated Policy will show a new \"Last updated\" date.\n\nWhere the law requires your consent to a material change, we will ask for it before the change takes effect.\n\n## 15. Language\n\nThis Privacy Policy is available in several languages. If there is any conflict between the versions, the English version prevails.\n\n## 16. Contact Us\n\nIf you have questions, requests, or complaints about this Privacy Policy or how we handle personal information, contact us:\n\nJoint controllers: Yoav Shamir, Michael Sigal, and Konstantine Staver\nPostal address: Bd. Traian 7/1, Chisinau, Republic of Moldova, 2060\nEmail: support@ragly.cloud\nWebsite: https://ragly.cloud\n\nWe review privacy requests and respond as required by applicable law.";
